      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(msteams): cap team-group-id cache with pruneMapToMaxSize",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `teamGroupIdCache` Map in `resolveTeamGroupId` had TTL-based expiry (10 min) but no size cap. A large Teams workspace with many distinct team IDs could accumulate entries faster than the TTL window, allowing unbounded growth.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdded a 500-entry cap via `pruneMapToMaxSize` — the shared SDK helper already used by 11 other files. The cap is applied after each successful cache insert.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo change for normal usage. Memory usage bounded at ~500 entries regardless of workspace size.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### `_teamGroupIdCacheForTest` proof — cache stays at 500 after 501+ inserts\n\nThe proof imports the real `_teamGroupIdCacheForTest` (exposed for testing), fills it with 501 entries while calling `pruneMapToMaxSize` on each insert (matching the production `resolveTeamGroupId` code path), and shows the cache stays capped at 500:\n\n```text\n$ node --import tsx graph-thread-proof.mjs 2>&1\n\n=== Proof: resolveTeamGroupId cache capped at 500 ===\n\n--- Fill cache with 501 entries ---\nCache size after 501 insert+prune cycles: 500\nHas team-0 (oldest):  false\nHas team-500 (newest): true\nOK: cache stays at 500, oldest entry evicted\n\n--- Second cycle (insert team-501) ---\nCache size after 502nd insert: 500\nOK: cache still capped\n\n=== Proof complete ===\n```\n\nThe same `pruneMapToMaxSize(teamGroupIdCache, 500)` is called in `resolveTeamGroupId` after each successful Graph API lookup.\n\n### Lint\n\n```text\n$ npx oxlint extensions/msteams/src/graph-thread.ts\n0 errors, 0 warnings\n```\n\nAI-assisted: built with Codex",
